    REMOVE DISPOSITION CHILD-MIRROR FIELDS - 2026-08-25. THE CONSTRUCTIVE HALF.

    STATUS: PREPARED, NOT DEPLOYED. Do not deploy without the user's explicit go-ahead.
    NOTHING IN THIS CHANGE WAS RUN AGAINST ANY ORG BY THE AGENT THAT WROTE IT - no deploy, no
    dry run, no `sf apex run`, no data query. Every claim below about org state is inference from
    the repo and is labelled as such.

    WHY: the user's decision, verbatim - "why have you created NDA, PSA and LOI fields on
    Disposition object - we don't need them. Remove them."

    WHAT IS BEING RETIRED: the whole child-mirror display idea. Between 2026-08-24 and 2026-08-25
    seventeen fields were added to Disposition__c so three stage-scoped Details sections on
    Disposition_Record_Page could render an LOI / PSA / NDA child's values as ordinary
    `Record.` fields (a FlexiPage fieldInstance cannot traverse a relationship, so the route was
    lookup -> spanning formula -> native fieldSection). The user does not want those values
    duplicated onto the parent. The child records are read on their OWN pages, reached from the
    loisList / contractReviewsList / ndasList related lists that remain on the page.

    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    🔴 THE TWO HALVES MUST BE ONE DEPLOY, AND CONSTRUCTIVE MUST LAND FIRST
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      - Disposition_Record_Page naming a fieldItem for a deleted field fails the deploy.
      - DPEG_Disposition_Edit / _View naming a fieldPermissions for a deleted field fails the
        deploy.
      - DispositionStageEntryService referencing DispositionPrimaryChildStampQueueable while that
        class is deleted fails to compile.
    `post-destructive-changes` lands everything in THIS file first, then performs the deletions
    in destructiveChangesPost.xml. That single ordering satisfies all three.

    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    WHAT IS IN HERE AND WHY
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      FlexiPage (1)  Disposition_Record_Page
        Loses THREE flexipage:fieldSection itemInstances (ndaDetails / loiDetails / psaDetails)
        and the NINE facet flexiPageRegions that fed them.
        🔴 AND IT LOSES THREE NE CRITERIA FROM flexipage_fieldSection'S OWN visibilityRule, WITH
        booleanFilter RENUMBERED FROM "1 AND 2 AND 3 AND 4 AND 5 AND 6 AND 7 AND 8" TO
        "1 AND 2 AND 3 AND 4 AND 5". THIS IS NOT TIDYING - IT IS THE WHOLE CORRECTNESS ARGUMENT.
        That page's `main` region partitions the Disposition_Stage__c value set: c_dispositionMain
        claims 5 stages by an OR-of-EQUAL allowlist, flexipage_fieldSection claims the rest by the
        AND-of-NE inverse. Removing the three single-EQUAL Details sections WITHOUT removing their
        stages from the NE chain would leave NDA / LOI / PSA claimed by nobody and excluded by the
        inverse - three stages rendering NO Details section at all, silently. That is the 2026-08-24
        "Release Materials fell through to neither surface" defect in mirror image. Post-change the
        partition is 5 + 6 = 11 again. Full arc is in the page file's own header.

      PermissionSet (3)
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit   drops 17 fieldPermissions (2 lookups editable + 15 read-only)
        DPEG_Disposition_View   drops the same 17, all read-only
        DPEG_Apex_Access        COMMENT-ONLY. Its DispositionChildDetailsController paragraph
                                described the native replacement that is now also gone.
        ⚠ A PERMISSION-SET DEPLOY REPLACES ITS ENTIRE fieldPermissions SET - it does not merge.
        These three files were edited by exact hunk, and nothing else in them was touched. If any
        other stream has uncommitted edits to the same three files, DIFF THEM BEFORE DEPLOYING:
        a merged file silently revokes the other stream's grants.
        ⚠ DPEG_Admin_Access is NOT in this payload. It grants Disposition__c.Primary_NDA__c, which
        SURVIVES (see below), and holds no grant for any of the 17.

      ApexClass (2)
        DispositionStageEntryService      LOI and PSA blocks lose their parent-stamp map build and
                                          their System.enqueueJob. Both blocks are back to "no
                                          parent stamp and no Queueable", which is what they were
                                          before 2026-08-25 and for the original reason: there is
                                          no Primary_LOI__c / Primary_PSA__c to write back to.
        DispositionStageEntryServiceTest  `loiAndPsaAutoCreateEachEnqueueOneParentStamp` is
                                          re-inverted to `loiAndPsaAutoCreateEnqueueNothing`
                                          (assert 0, its pre-08-25 form), and
                                          `primaryChildStampQueueableIsInertOnAnEmptyOrNullMap`
                                          is DELETED - there is no class left for it to cover.
        ⚠ BOTH MUST BE IN THE PAYLOAD. the tests flag runs the ORG's copy of a test class, so a
        committed-but-undeployed test method silently never runs and the deploy still reports
        success. The test class is the only falsifier for the enqueue count in either direction.

      CustomField (3) - ALL THREE ARE COMMENT / description CHANGES, NOT SHAPE CHANGES
        Disposition__c.Primary_NDA__c        SURVIVES. Its header claimed "downstream automation
                                             resolves the NDA it acts on THROUGH this lookup" -
                                             that is now FALSE and is retracted in place. A full
                                             repo grep on 2026-08-25 found NO reader: the
                                             "downstream automation" is the OPPORTUNITY twin's
                                             (NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression reads
                                             Opportunity.Primary_NDA__r.NDA_Signed__c). See the
                                             field file for why it is retained anyway.
        LOI__c.Selected_Offer__c             UNAFFECTED by the removal; its comment cross-referenced
        Contract_Review__c.Selected_Offer__c Primary_LOI__c / Primary_PSA__c and the one-off
                                             backfill, both of which are gone. Amended, not
                                             rewritten. These two are LINKS to real child records,
                                             not mirrors of one onto the parent - which is exactly
                                             the distinction the user's decision turns on.

    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    🔴 THINGS DELIBERATELY **NOT** IN EITHER HALF
