    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    ⚠ TWO THINGS TO CHECK BEFORE RUNNING THIS
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    1. DOES THE ORG ACTUALLY HAVE ALL 17 FIELDS? A destructive delete naming a component the org
       does not have fails the deploy unless `the ignore-warnings flag` is passed. The repo's evidence
       says yes - Disposition_Record_Page was RETRIEVED from the org at commit 472155f WITH the
       three Details sections in it, and a FlexiPage cannot name a field that does not exist -
       but that is inference, not a measurement. Confirm with a describe, or pass
       `the ignore-warnings flag`.
       ⚠ manifest/native-loi-psa/package.xml says "STATUS: PREPARED, NOT DEPLOYED" for the eleven
       LOI/PSA fields. That status line is STALE if the 472155f retrieve means what it appears to
       mean. Trust the retrieve over the status line, and check.
    2. ORDERING INSIDE THE DESTRUCTIVE HALF. Deleting Primary_LOI__c / Primary_PSA__c while a
       formula field still spans them fails. Both are in the same destructive package and the
       formulas are listed FIRST; the Metadata API resolves intra-package dependencies, but if it
       refuses, split into two deploys - formulas first, lookups second.

    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    HOW TO DEPLOY IT
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    🔴 THE RUNNABLE COMMANDS LIVE IN DEPLOY.md BESIDE THIS FILE, NOT HERE, AND THAT IS NOT A
    STYLE CHOICE. An XML comment may not contain a double hyphen, so every `sf` flag written
    inside one makes the manifest itself unparseable - which is exactly the shape of latent trap
    this repo keeps paying for, and manifest/native-loi-psa/package.xml already carries it.
    Flags are therefore named WITHOUT their leading dashes in this comment.

    Shape: `sf project deploy start`, with `manifest` pointing at this file, `post-destructive-changes`
    pointing at destructiveChangesPost.xml, `target-org usman-dpeg`,
    `test-level RunSpecifiedTests`, `tests DispositionStageEntryServiceTest`, plus `dry-run` and
    `wait 60`. The real deploy is the same command with the dry-run flag removed.

    ⚠ A GREEN DRY RUN IS WEAKER EVIDENCE THAN IT LOOKS, TWICE OVER, AND BOTH TRAPS ARE DOCUMENTED
    IN THIS REPO'S HISTORY:
      - Byte-identical components report `Unchanged` and are SKIPPED rather than validated. That
        applies to DPEG_Apex_Access here, which is a comment-only edit.
      - "N/N deployed, 0 errors" has been observed on a deploy that rolled everything back:
        `numberComponentsDeployed` is a PRE-rollback tally, and RunSpecifiedTests can fail on
        per-class 75% coverage through `codeCoverageWarnings` that no error counter surfaces.
        Read the coverage section of the result, not just the error count.
    ⚠ IF PER-CLASS COVERAGE IS THE BLOCKER, RE-RUN AT test-level RunLocalTests. Deleting
    `primaryChildStampQueueableIsInertOnAnEmptyOrNullMap` removes coverage from
    DispositionStageEntryService's LOI/PSA enqueue lines - but those lines are deleted in the same
    change, so the ratio should improve, not fall.
